Grove PATCH-28: price ZEPH as zephyr-protocol, not "zephyr"

The console showed the operator's 67.266218166684 ZEPH as $1.19 while the
wallet showed $27.08 for the same balance. Neither number was a bug in the
balance -- both sides read 67.266218166684 from the same wallet-rpc. They
disagreed about what a ZEPH is worth, by a factor of 22.7.

getExchangeName sends chainparams[coin]["name"] to CoinGecko as an id, and
Zephyr's chainparams name is "zephyr". That id exists on CoinGecko and is a
DIFFERENT ASSET. Measured 2026-09-05:

    /simple/price?ids=zephyr,zephyr-protocol,zano,bitcoin-cash
    {"zephyr":{"usd":0.01772103},"zephyr-protocol":{"usd":0.402475},
     "zano":{"usd":6.7},"bitcoin-cash":{"usd":249.6}}

    67.266218166684 * 0.01772103 = $1.19   <- what the console showed
    67.266218166684 * 0.402475   = $27.07  <- what the wallet showed

So the console was not stale or rounding; it was pricing a namesake token.
The wallet has used "zephyr-protocol" since its own price map was written
(src/wallets/usd-prices.ts).

This function already carries exactly this kind of exception -- BCH's chain
name is "bitcoincash" but its CoinGecko id is "bitcoin-cash", and FIRO's is
"zcoin" -- so ZEPH joins that list rather than getting a new mechanism. Every
other Grove coin was checked against the live API the same way and resolves
correctly on its chainparams name (bitcoin, litecoin, dash, dogecoin,
particl, monero, wownero, zano, decred, namecoin, pivx).

The wrong price is not cosmetic here: lookupFiatRates feeds the offer book's
rate columns and the AMM page as well as the wallet cards, so a coin priced
at 4% of its value reads as a spectacular bargain everywhere it appears.

Upstream candidate: yes, if Zephyr lands upstream -- it is a one-line id
correction of exactly the shape already present for two other coins.

Rebased 2026-10-06 onto basicswap v0.19.0 (277b46b0278f1cc76199f7e847988647a1b36e38). The function this patched is gone. v0.18.10 moved every oracle id into the coin's chainparams `rate_ids` (56153e3a), and oracles.getExchangeName reads `chainparams[coin]["rate_ids"]` with no fallback to the chain name. So the patch now adds `rate_ids` to the zephyr and zano chainparams, which PATCH-13 and PATCH-15 create. ZEPH's CoinGecko id stays "zephyr-protocol". ZANO resolved on its chain name until v0.18.9; it now needs its own entry, or every oracle fetch that includes it raises KeyError and, for CoinGecko, which is asked for all coins at once, returns no price for any coin. MEXC and CoinPaprika ids were checked against the live APIs on 2026-10-06 (ZEPH ~$0.363 and ZANO ~$5.26 on all three); Kraken, KuCoin and neroswap list neither coin. `verify-coin-price-ids.py` reads the ids through oracles.getExchangeName. The diff below is regenerated.

